---

# TICKETING_UI_UX_REVIEW

**Feature:** `ticketing-ui-ux-denali`  
**Branch:** `cursor/ticketing-ui-ux`  
**Base:** `feature/ticketing-system` @ `b29244f2` (merge-base)  
**Date:** 2026-09-04

## Current strengths

- Ticketing is a **primary** member portal module in Denali manifest (`/me/tickets`, nav tier primary).
- Operator uses **split-pane command center** (inbox 3fr + detail 2fr) — aligns with industry inbox patterns (Zendesk Agent Home split view).
- Member conversation uses **author-aligned bubbles** with RTL-safe `margin-inline` rules.
- Operator separates **public vs internal** timelines in markup (`data-visibility`).
- Shared **member_notifications** bell — no duplicate ticket-only notification UI.
- Functional Playwright smoke + Axe specs exist for portal and operator ticketing.

## Placement decisions

| # | Decision | Rationale |
|---|----------|-----------|
| 1 | Keep Tickets in **primary portal nav** (not buried in More) | Support is a core member self-service path; manifest already places it at primary tier. |
| 2 | **No open-ticket count in nav badge** (this phase) | Avoid duplicate signal with notification bell; open count belongs in list filters, not nav chrome. |
| 3 | **No dashboard ticket summary widget** (this phase) | Member home focuses on trips/registrations; ticket CTA lives on list empty state + nav. |
| 4 | List shows subject, status, category, priority, message count, last activity; detail shows full timeline + composer | List = scan; detail = act. |
| 5 | Primary action by state: open/pending → **reply**; resolved → **reopen**; closed → read-only | Matches support portal conventions. |
| 6 | Status via **icon + label + semantic color** (not color alone); priority as secondary meta | WCAG 1.4.1; banners reinforce state in plain language. |
| 7 | Attachments on mobile: **filename link** in message bubble, full-width tap target | Avoid thumbnail clutter on narrow viewports. |
| 8 | Internal notes: **warning-tinted panel + border** separate from public thread | Prevents operator confusion (Zendesk/Intercom pattern). |
| 9 | Operator: **keep split-pane** on desktop; bottom sheet on mobile | Already implemented; matches split-view efficiency research. |
| 10 | Bulk toolbar: **always visible when mutating**, confirm on destructive bulk status | Discoverable without cluttering rows; confirm before resolve/close. |
| 11 | Notifications: **bell only** for unread; tickets nav does not duplicate bell | MNI-001 single inbox authority. |

## Defect remediation matrix

| ID | Sev | Surface | Observed defect | Remediation | Verification |
|----|-----|---------|-----------------|-------------|--------------|
| UX-01 | P1 | Portal list | Filter chips lacked active/hover styling; unicode ◎/● markers confused | Removed unicode markers; `aria-pressed` + Denali chip tokens | Portal screenshot + Axe smoke |
| UX-02 | P1 | Portal list/detail | Status badges lacked semantic color hierarchy | Token-based badge colors with icon + label | Portal screenshot + Axe smoke |
| UX-03 | P1 | Portal detail | Status banner unstyled — weak state communication | Semantic status banners per state | Portal screenshot + Axe smoke |
| UX-04 | P1 | Portal create | Raw form controls; tour/registration UUID fields exposed | Advanced `<details>` disclosure; Denali form field spacing | Portal screenshot + smoke |
| UX-05 | P1 | Portal detail | Success actions not announced (`aria-live` only showed errors) | `replySuccess` / `reopenSuccess` in `aria-live="polite"` | Portal smoke + Axe |
| UX-06 | P1 | Operator detail | Internal notes visually weak (3px border only) | Warning-tinted panel + border on internal messages/composer | Operator detail screenshot + smoke |
| UX-07 | P1 | Operator inbox | Emoji 📎 attachment indicator — poor a11y | Text label + `aria-label` | Operator inbox screenshot + smoke |
| UX-08 | P1 | Operator bulk | No confirm before bulk resolve/close | `OperatorConfirmDialog` for bulk `resolved`/`closed` | `operator-ticketing-bulk-confirm.spec.ts` |
| UX-09 | P2 | Operator detail | Resolve/close lacked explicit confirm | Per-action `OperatorConfirmDialog` | Operator inbox smoke |
| UX-10 | P2 | Operator CSS | Hardcoded hex colors instead of tokens | `var(--*)` + `color-mix` contrast fixes | Operator Axe smoke |
| UX-11 | P2 | Portal | Empty state / form field spacing inconsistent | Denali `member-pages.css` ticketing block | Portal screenshots |
| UX-12 | P3 | Operator inbox | Row meta dense on 360px | Existing wrap rules retained; contrast tweak only | Operator screenshot @ 360×800 |

## Evidence capture (before/after)

`TICKETING_UI_UX_PHASE` alone only selects the output folder — it does **not** change the running code. Use the deterministic capture script:

```bash
node scripts/capture-ticketing-ui-ux-evidence.mjs
```

- **Before:** temporarily checks out merge-base UI files on the locked branch, then captures (see script)
- **After:** current `HEAD` on `cursor/ticketing-ui-ux`
- **Output:** `/opt/cursor/artifacts/screenshots/ticketing-ui-ux/{before,after}/`
- **Manifest:** `hash-manifest.json` with SHA-256 per file; script exits non-zero if any pair is byte-identical

## Rejected alternatives

- **Ticket-only notification tab** — violates MNI-001.
- **Full-page operator detail navigation** — regresses triage efficiency vs split-pane.
- **Moving tickets to secondary “More” hub** — reduces discoverability for club support.
- **New bespoke design system** — extend Denali `member-pages.css` + operator tokens only.

## Acceptance criteria

1. BEFORE/AFTER screenshots at 1440×900, 1280×800, 768×1024, 390×844, 360×800 for portal list, new form, nav; operator inbox + detail. Capture via `node scripts/capture-ticketing-ui-ux-evidence.mjs` (worktree before @ `b29244f2`, after @ HEAD).
2. Filter chips show clear active state without unicode-only markers.
3. Status badges and banners use semantic tokens with icon + text.
4. Create form hides tour/registration IDs behind optional advanced disclosure.
5. Member reply/reopen announces success via `aria-live`.
6. Operator internal notes visually distinct from public messages.
7. Bulk resolve/close requires `OperatorConfirmDialog`.
8. Attachment indicator uses accessible text label.
9. Portal + operator Playwright smoke and Axe specs pass.
10. No API / RLS / notification architecture changes.

